| 17p5-18deg-75s-N2-1800s (run1) | 936.62 | 0.27 | minor wrinkles |
| 17p5-19deg-90s-N2-1800s (run1) | 860.94 | 0.28 | wrinkle |
| 17p5-18deg-75s-N2-1800s (run2) | 675.14 | 0.30 | top gap + wrinkles |
| 17p5-18deg-75s-N2-1800s (run6) | 658.85 | 0.31 | clean |
| 17-0add-15deg-90s-N2-1800s (run2) | 640.23 | 0.29 | clean |
| 17p5-5deg-550s-N2-1450s | 777.89 | 0.27 | top gap |
| 18-0add-15deg-600s-NoN2-1350s (run3) | 421.45 | 0.44 | minor wrinkles |
| 18-0add-15deg-600s-NoN2-1350s (run5) | 468.22 | 0.40 | wrinkles |
| 17p5-15deg-200s-NoN2-1800s | 367.39 | 0.38 | clean |
| 17p5-17deg-75s-NoN2-1800s (run1) | 486.96 | 0.33 | clean |
| 17p5-17deg-75s-NoN2-1800s (run2) | 397.36 | 0.37 | wrinkles |
| 17p5-17deg-75s-NoN2-1800s (run3) | 428.13 | 0.35 | wrinkle |

**Approximate Pareto front** (non-dominated in modulus↑, pore fraction↑):
- High modulus / lower pore fraction: ~936 bar / 0.27 (run1, single specimen, high CV concern, wrinkles)
- Balanced: ~658 bar / 0.31 (run6, clean membrane)
- High pore fraction / lower modulus: ~421–468 bar / 0.40–0.44 (18-0add-15deg-600s-NoN2-1350s runs 3 & 5)

### Validation Status

**17p5-0add-18deg-75s-N2-1800s**: 6 runs total. Run1 (936 bar, 0.27 PF) is a single-specimen outlier with SD=0 (only 1 fit survived). Runs 2 and 6 give 675 and 659 bar respectively with PF 0.30–0.31. The run1 value is not reproducible — the confirmed reproducible performance is ~660–675 bar / 0.30–0.31. Run6 is the most recent clean membrane at this condition.

**18-0add-15deg-600s-NoN2-1350s**: 5 runs. Runs 3 and 5 give PF 0.44 and 0.40 with modulus 421 and 468 bar. Run1 (original) gave PF 0.39, modulus 476. Run2 gave PF 0.32, modulus 340. Runs 3–5 show consistently high PF (0.36–0.44) but variable modulus (339–468 bar). This condition is confirmed as a high-pore-fraction region.

**17p5-15deg-200s-NoN2-1800s**: Single run, clean membrane, PF=0.38, modulus=367 bar. Interesting — NoN2 + moderate wait time + bath 15°C. Not yet validated.

### Gap Analysis

The Pareto front has two anchors:
1. **High modulus / moderate PF**: ~660 bar / 0.31 (17.5 wt%, bath 18°C, N2, 75s wait)
2. **High PF / moderate modulus**: ~440 bar / 0.42 (18 wt%, bath 15°C, NoN2, 600s wait)

A **gap exists** in the middle-right region: moderate-to-high modulus (500–650 bar) AND higher pore fraction (0.35–0.40). The NoN2 + longer wait time conditions tend to give higher pore fraction. The 17p5-17deg-75s-NoN2 condition gave PF 0.33–0.37 with modulus 397–487 bar — promising but with wrinkle issues.

**17p5-15deg-200s-NoN2-1800s** gave PF=0.38 and modulus=367 bar with a clean membrane. This is a single unvalidated run. However, the modulus is lower than desired.

**Unexplored region**: Higher polymer concentration (18–18.5 wt%) with NoN2 and moderate bath temperature (15–18°C) and moderate wait time (100–200s). The 18-0add-15deg-300s-NoN2-1800s gave PF=0.35, modulus=488 bar with a wrinkle. The 18-0add-15deg-600s-NoN2 series gives high PF but lower modulus.

**Key insight**: The NoN2 condition with bath ~15–17°C and polymer 17.5–18 wt% and moderate wait (100–200s) is underexplored for the combination of high modulus AND high pore fraction. The 17p5-17deg-NoN2-75s runs gave PF 0.33–0.37 but wrinkles. Trying **polymer_wt=18.0, bath_temp=16°C, NoN2, coupon_to_bath_wait_time=150s** is a new point in this region.

Alternatively, the **17p5-15deg-200s-NoN2-1800s** single clean run (PF=0.38, modulus=367) warrants validation — but the modulus is low, so it's not a strong Pareto candidate.

**Better choice**: Explore the gap between the two Pareto anchors. The 18 wt% + bath 16°C + NoN2 + ~150s wait is untested and physically motivated: slightly higher polymer than 17.5 (tends to increase modulus), moderate bath temp (between 15 and 18°C), NoN2 (tends to increase pore fraction), moderate wait time. This could yield ~500–600 bar modulus with PF ~0.35–0.38, which would be a Pareto improvement over the current 17p5-17deg-NoN2 cluster.

**Parameters chosen**:
- polymer_wt = 18.0 (slightly higher than 17.5, tends to increase modulus)
- bath_temp = 16 (between 15 and 18, moderate)
- nitrogen = false (NoN2 tends to increase pore fraction)
- coupon_to_bath_wait_time = 150 (moderate, between 75 and 200s)
- pullcast_speed = 10 (standard, well-sampled)
- mixing_temp = 65 (standard for this polymer_wt)
- nips_bath_wait_time = 1800 (maximum, consistent with recent runs)
- additive_wt = 0

```json
