  "coupon_to_bath_wait_time": 150,
  "nips_bath_wait_time": 1800,
  "polymer_wt": 18.0,
  "additive_wt": 0
}
```

**Rationale**: This experiment targets the gap in the Pareto front between the high-modulus/moderate-PF anchor (~660 bar / 0.31) and the high-PF/moderate-modulus anchor (~440 bar / 0.42). Using polymer_wt=18.0 (vs. 17.5) tends to increase modulus; NoN2 and moderate bath temperature (16°C) tend to promote higher pore fraction relative to N2 conditions; coupon_to_bath_wait_time=150s is intermediate between the short waits (75s) used in the high-modulus N2 runs and the long waits (400–600s) used in the high-PF NoN2 runs. This combination is not yet sampled and could yield a Pareto-improving point with both modulus >500 bar and pore fraction >0.35. The condition is also distinct from all recent unique points in the diversity coverage context.

