[2026-11-04 14:56:42] LLM suggestion: ## Analysis

### Pareto Front Review (both objectives measured)

Filtering to experiments with both Elastic Modulus and Pore Fraction measured:

| Condition | Modulus (bar) | Pore Fraction | Quality |
|---|---|---|---|
| 17p5-18deg-75s-N2-1800s (run1) | 936.62 | 0.27 | minor wrinkles |
| 17p5-19deg-90s-N2-1800s (run1) | 860.94 | 0.28 | wrinkle |
| 17p5-18deg-75s-N2-1800s (run2) | 675.14 | 0.30 | wrinkle/gap |
| 17p5-18deg-75s-N2-1800s (run6) | 658.85 | 0.31 | clean ✓ |
| 17-15deg-90s-N2-1800s (run2) | 640.23 | 0.29 | clean ✓ |
| 18-0add-15deg-600s-NoN2-1350s (run3) | 421.45 | **0.44** | minor wrinkles |
| 18-0add-15deg-600s-NoN2-1350s (run5) | 468.22 | **0.40** | wrinkles |
| 17p5-15deg-200s-NoN2-1800s | 367.39 | **0.38** | clean ✓ |
| 17p5-17deg-75s-NoN2-1800s (run2) | 397.36 | 0.37 | wrinkles |
| 18-12deg-90s-N2-1800s (run2) | 349.37 | **0.47** | wrinkles/gap |

**Approximate Pareto front** (non-dominated in modulus × pore fraction):
- High modulus / lower pore fraction: ~936 bar / 0.27 (run1, single specimen, high CV, wrinkles)
- Balanced: ~658 bar / 0.31 (run6, clean, 1 run)
- High pore fraction / lower modulus: ~421 bar / 0.44 (run3, minor wrinkles); ~349 bar / 0.47 (run2, defects)

### Validation Status Assessment

**17p5-0add-18deg-75s-N2-1800s**: 6 runs total. Run1 (936 bar, 0.27 PF) is a single-specimen outlier with SD=0 (only 1 fit survived), high apparent modulus. Run2 (675 bar, 0.30) has wrinkle/gap. Run6 (658 bar, 0.31) is clean with good CV=0.13. Runs 4 and 5 failed to yield modulus. The run1 value is not reproducible across the series — the mean of runs with valid modulus is ~756 bar but with high scatter. This condition has been extensively repeated; the modulus is genuinely variable.

**18-0add-15deg-600s-NoN2-1350s**: 5 runs. Runs 1 (original), 2, 3, 4, 5 all have modulus and pore fraction. Means: modulus ~417 bar (range 340–476), pore fraction ~0.38 (range 0.32–0.44). This is a reproducible high-pore-fraction candidate but with moderate modulus. Run3 achieved 0.44 PF — the highest clean-ish result.

**17p5-15deg-200s-NoN2-1800s**: Single run, clean membrane, 367 bar / 0.38 PF. Not validated.

### Key Observations

The Pareto frontier shows a clear trade-off: conditions favoring high modulus (bath_temp ~18–19°C, polymer_wt 17–17.5, N2, short wait) give ~600–900 bar but PF ~0.27–0.31. Conditions favoring high pore fraction (longer wait, no N2, bath_temp ~15°C, polymer_wt 18) give PF ~0.38–0.47 but modulus ~350–470 bar.

**Gap in the Pareto front**: Is there a condition that could achieve both ~500–600 bar modulus AND ~0.36–0.40 pore fraction? The data suggests this region is underexplored. The `17p5-17deg-NoN2-75s-1800s` condition (run1: 486 bar / 0.33 PF, clean) and `17p5-17deg-NoN2-120s-1800s` (582 bar / 0.36 PF, wrinkles/gap) hint that bath_temp ~17°C + no N2 + polymer_wt 17.5 might be promising for balanced performance.

**`17p5-17deg-NoN2-120s-1800s`** gave 582 bar / 0.36 PF but had a bottom coverage gap and wrinkles. Only 1 run. This is an interesting candidate but needs validation.

**`17p5-15deg-200s-NoN2-1800s`** gave 367 bar / 0.38 PF with a clean membrane. Only 1 run.

**Under-explored region**: polymer_wt ~17.5, bath_temp ~17°C, no N2, moderate wait (~75–120s), pullcast_speed 10, mixing_temp 65. The run1 of `17p5-17deg-NoN2-75s-1800s` was clean and defect-free with 486 bar / 0.33 PF. Run2 had wrinkles and 397 bar / 0.37 PF. Run3 had wrinkles and 428 bar / 0.35 PF. The mean across 3 runs: ~437 bar / 0.35 PF — a modest but reproducible balanced point.

**Better exploration target**: Slightly increasing polymer_wt to 18.0 with bath_temp ~17°C, no N2, short-moderate wait (~75s) has not been tried. Higher polymer concentration tends to increase modulus; bath_temp ~17°C and no N2 tend to increase pore fraction. This combination could push toward the balanced Pareto region (~500+ bar, ~0.35+ PF).

**Alternatively**: `18-0add-15deg-200s-NoN2-1800s` — similar to the clean `17p5-15deg-200s-NoN2-1800s` but with higher polymer_wt (18 vs 17.5) to boost modulus while retaining the high-PF conditions. This is a new point not yet tried.

### Recommendation

I recommend exploring **polymer_wt=18.0, bath_temp=17°C, no N2, coupon_to_bath_wait_time=75s** — a new combination that:
- Uses higher polymer concentration than the 17.5 wt% runs at bath_temp=17°C (which gave ~430–580 bar / 0.33–0.37 PF) to push modulus higher
- Retains bath_temp=17°C and no N2 (conditions associated with elevated pore fraction vs. N2 runs)
- Uses 75s wait (short enough to avoid excessive skin formation, consistent with the clean run1 of 17p5-17deg-NoN2-75s)
- pullcast_speed=10 (well-established, consistent with recent experiments)
- mixing_temp=65 (standard for this polymer_wt)
- nips_bath_wait_time=1800s (maximum, consistent with recent high-quality runs)

This is a genuinely new point (18.0 wt%, bath_temp=17°C, no N2, 75s wait) not previously sampled, targeting the under-explored balanced region of the Pareto front.

